WEBVTT

00:01.700 --> 00:04.935
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.035 --> 00:08.321
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.355 --> 00:11.891
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.909 --> 00:14.894
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.912 --> 00:18.397
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.415 --> 00:21.701
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.735 --> 00:23.252
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.287 --> 00:24.620
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.655 --> 00:26.976
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.016 --> 00:37.250
Hey, Brian,
have you seen the remote?

00:37.284 --> 00:38.785
I want to watch
The Weather Channel.

00:38.819 --> 00:40.319
There are tornados
in the Midwest,

00:40.354 --> 00:42.088
and I like watching
poor people scramble

00:42.122 --> 00:43.524
to save
what little they have.

00:43.558 --> 00:45.159
Uh, I don't know
where the remote is.

00:45.193 --> 00:46.493
All right,
I'll find it myself.

00:48.496 --> 00:51.031
Oh, my God, my old harmonica!

00:51.066 --> 00:53.333
I'm gonna play this
really loud tonight

00:53.368 --> 00:55.769
to get back
at our Armenian neighbors.

00:55.804 --> 00:57.371
(kids laughing inside, knocks)

00:57.405 --> 00:58.572
Hey.

00:58.606 --> 00:59.973
Hey, looks like
a fun party.

01:00.008 --> 01:02.276
Um, hey, listen, it's
2:00 in the morning.

01:02.310 --> 01:04.945
Uh, when is your five-year-old
gonna go to sleep?

01:04.979 --> 01:06.080
Soon, very soon.

01:06.114 --> 01:08.649
You want weird food
wrapped in weird leaves?

01:08.683 --> 01:10.317
Yeah, look, I'm guessing
there's some kind of

01:10.351 --> 01:12.586
soccer match from your
home country going on,

01:12.620 --> 01:14.321
and I get that, I do.

01:14.355 --> 01:16.657
But, uh, some of us
are trying to sleep,

01:16.691 --> 01:18.725
and I could almost
deal with the noise,

01:18.760 --> 01:21.061
but it's the
cologne, all right?

01:21.096 --> 01:24.064
I can smell it in my bed, and
I live two houses from here.

01:24.099 --> 01:26.733
That's how powerful
it is, okay?

01:26.768 --> 01:28.035
That's how powerful it is.

01:28.069 --> 01:29.803
You like it?

01:29.838 --> 01:31.304
Yeah, I kind
of like it.

01:35.876 --> 01:37.443
Okay, so I know
you're a harmonica,

01:37.478 --> 01:39.479
but right now
you're a 40-year-old woman

01:39.513 --> 01:41.347
with a good body
in a hotel pool.

01:41.381 --> 01:43.049
(high-pitched voice):
Hey, everybody, look at me.

01:43.083 --> 01:45.718
I work out seven days a
for these five minutes.

01:45.752 --> 01:47.353
Your attention
is going to keep me

01:47.387 --> 01:48.955
from swallowing
a bottle of pills.

01:48.989 --> 01:51.124
LOIS (in distance):
Hey, everyone, I made brownies!

01:51.158 --> 01:52.391
(gasps)
I better hurry up.

01:52.426 --> 01:53.693
I'm gonna miss the show.

01:53.727 --> 01:55.695
(crying):
What did I do?

01:55.729 --> 01:57.730
What did I do?

02:00.667 --> 02:02.869
I love brownie day.

02:05.906 --> 02:07.574
Hey, so, uh,

02:07.609 --> 02:09.810
I'm digging a hole
under the fence in the backyard.

02:09.844 --> 02:11.145
Brian, you have a car.

02:11.179 --> 02:12.446
You don't have to escape.

02:12.480 --> 02:14.081
Just don't (bleep)
say anything, okay?

02:14.115 --> 02:16.583
Oh, you know what, hang on, I
left my harmonica in the tub.

02:16.618 --> 02:18.252
I think Peter's in there
taking a bath.

02:18.286 --> 02:19.987
PETER:
Aah! Son of a bitch!

02:20.021 --> 02:21.922
What the hell did
I just sit on?

02:21.956 --> 02:24.091
Where is it?
Where's my harmonica?

02:24.125 --> 02:25.159
It's not here!

02:25.193 --> 02:26.426
Peter, have you seen
Stewie's harmonica?

02:26.461 --> 02:27.561
It was in the tub.

02:27.595 --> 02:29.696
Oh, my God, it
was in the tub,

02:29.731 --> 02:31.398
and now it's
in my butt!

02:31.432 --> 02:33.267
No!

02:33.301 --> 02:35.769
Stewie, Daddy needs
your tiny hands

02:35.803 --> 02:38.572
for a very
special project.

02:42.777 --> 02:45.245
Well, good heavens, that's
something, isn't it?

02:45.280 --> 02:47.347
By the way, Mr. Griffin,
regarding your X-rays,

02:47.382 --> 02:48.949
we're making a
coffee table book.

02:48.983 --> 02:50.417
Can you sign this
release, please?

02:50.451 --> 02:53.387
Okay, but first can we address
my husband's situation?

02:53.421 --> 02:55.255
Well, the harmonica's
up there pretty good.

02:55.290 --> 02:57.324
Unfortunately, removing
it would require

02:57.358 --> 02:58.825
a very expensive surgery

02:58.860 --> 03:01.328
that's not covered by your
T.G.I. Friday's gift card.

03:01.362 --> 03:03.230
(harmonica plays, giggles)

03:03.264 --> 03:04.731
What was that?
I don't know,

03:04.766 --> 03:07.668
(sniffs) but suddenly it smells
like John Popper in here.

03:07.702 --> 03:09.703
That was me.
I got musical farts.

03:09.737 --> 03:11.271
(plays a scale)

03:11.306 --> 03:13.807
(giggles)
Holy crap, this is awesome.

03:13.841 --> 03:15.509
I will not allow
this opportunity

03:15.543 --> 03:16.810
to go to waste.

03:20.648 --> 03:22.382
Hey, Lois, how
was your day?

03:22.417 --> 03:24.585
Terrible. I accidentally
backed over a kid

03:24.619 --> 03:26.587
in the grocery store
parking lot.

03:26.621 --> 03:28.255
(plays blues riff)

03:28.289 --> 03:29.856
Peter, I'm serious.

03:29.891 --> 03:32.160
I ran right over
the soft part of the face.

03:32.194 --> 03:33.728
I had to run away.

03:33.762 --> 03:36.130
I ditched the car
and jumped on a passing train.

03:36.165 --> 03:38.166
(plays Western music)

03:40.169 --> 03:41.536
I was so scared.

03:41.570 --> 03:43.638
I didn't get off
until I was in the South.

03:43.672 --> 03:46.507
(plays "Dixieland")

03:46.542 --> 03:47.942
What'd you do today?

03:47.977 --> 03:49.410
I pushed a boy
behind your car

03:49.445 --> 03:51.579
so I could do all
this harmonica stuff.

03:53.949 --> 03:54.916
(snoring)

03:54.950 --> 03:56.150
(whispering):
All right, Chris,

03:56.185 --> 03:58.586
Meg loves to listen
to music when she sleeps.

03:58.621 --> 04:00.622
Let's see how she likes this.

04:02.358 --> 04:05.093
Uh, Dad, I don't think
that's how it works.

04:11.367 --> 04:13.935
This had nothing to do
with the harmonica.

04:17.973 --> 04:21.276
Everybody, brace yourselves,
'cause I have got big news.

04:21.310 --> 04:23.144
I have been selected
to be a contestant

04:23.178 --> 04:24.612
<i>on America's Got Talent!</i>

04:24.647 --> 04:27.315
And they're gonna fly us all
to America for the show!

04:27.349 --> 04:29.217
What?! Oh, my God!

04:29.251 --> 04:31.051
(Italian accent):
Finally, we make'a da dreams

04:31.085 --> 04:32.719
come true in America!

04:32.754 --> 04:34.554
I am gonna make
this family proud,

04:34.589 --> 04:35.856
and not just you guys,

04:35.890 --> 04:38.325
but that old painting
of my ancestor in the attic.

04:38.359 --> 04:40.294
I did it! I'm
gonna be on TV!

04:40.328 --> 04:41.728
Did you kill the others?

04:41.763 --> 04:43.397
I shan't!
You must.

04:43.431 --> 04:46.166
(sighs) I'm gonna go talk to
the statue in the basement.

04:46.200 --> 04:47.734
Did you kill
the painting?

04:47.769 --> 04:49.836
This place is a nuthouse.

04:52.774 --> 04:55.476
(cheering)

04:55.511 --> 04:57.645
<i>Yo, welcome back
to America's Got Talent!</i>

04:57.680 --> 04:59.113
Let's welcome
our next performer,

04:59.148 --> 05:01.749
here to play the harmonica,
Peter Griffin.

05:01.784 --> 05:03.651
(applause)

05:03.686 --> 05:04.819
Hi.

05:04.853 --> 05:06.988
So, where are you from, Peter?

05:07.022 --> 05:09.490
Um, I'm from
Quahog, Rhode Island.

05:09.525 --> 05:10.658
(Lois whooping)

05:10.693 --> 05:12.026
Quahog!

05:12.061 --> 05:13.361
(chuckles):
That's my family.

05:13.395 --> 05:15.830
My wife daytime drinks
on vacation.

05:15.864 --> 05:18.399
Okay, Peter,
let's hear what you've got.

05:18.434 --> 05:20.802
("Sanford and Son Theme"
playing)

05:22.805 --> 05:24.806
(snapping to music)

05:34.083 --> 05:35.416
(harmonica playing)

05:36.618 --> 05:38.619
(harmonica continues)

05:43.125 --> 05:44.192
Wow, he's nailing it.

05:44.226 --> 05:45.360
I know, shut up.

05:54.136 --> 05:55.370
(cheering)

05:55.404 --> 05:57.405
(farts, music stops)

05:58.407 --> 05:59.874
(gasping)

05:59.908 --> 06:01.809
Well, there goes
my music career.

06:01.844 --> 06:03.978
I wonder if I can get
my old job back

06:04.012 --> 06:06.247
painting kids' faces
at birthday parties.

06:06.281 --> 06:07.949
There you go, Timmy.

06:07.983 --> 06:09.450
Sir, you're gonna have
to leave.

06:09.485 --> 06:11.219
You're just drawing penises
with a Sharpie

06:11.253 --> 06:12.420
on children's faces.

06:12.454 --> 06:14.422
I don't know how
to draw a cat.

06:18.995 --> 06:20.729
Hi, I'm Amanda.

06:20.764 --> 06:22.731
I'm Chris.
You look nice,

06:22.766 --> 06:24.700
so I'll blow my burps
the other way.

06:24.734 --> 06:25.868
(laughs)

06:25.902 --> 06:27.269
You're funny.

06:27.303 --> 06:28.437
Oh, thanks.

06:28.471 --> 06:30.272
Usually people
just find me awkward.

06:30.306 --> 06:32.341
I have a hard time
with small talk.

06:32.375 --> 06:34.643
Did you find everything
you were looking for?

06:34.677 --> 06:36.044
Eh, I did all right

06:36.079 --> 06:38.199
for a guy who just had his
first homosexual experience

06:38.214 --> 06:40.048
with his guitar teacher.

06:43.420 --> 06:45.454
All right, guys,
keep an eye out for our stuff.

06:45.488 --> 06:47.756
I got tired of not being able
to find my bags,

06:47.791 --> 06:49.625
so I tied a vaguely
Hanna-Barbera-looking

06:49.659 --> 06:51.093
character to it.

06:51.127 --> 06:53.896
This trip was imposserous!

06:53.930 --> 06:55.330
There we go.

06:55.365 --> 06:58.100
I really enjoyed sitting next
to you on the plane, Chris.

06:58.134 --> 06:59.168
Me, too.

06:59.202 --> 07:00.502
I'm sorry I screamed

07:00.537 --> 07:02.771
when that guy from India
got up to stretch.

07:02.806 --> 07:04.706
Look, I'm having brunch
tomorrow with my grandparents

07:04.741 --> 07:06.208
at the Barrington
Country Club.

07:06.242 --> 07:07.443
Maybe your family
could join us.

07:07.477 --> 07:09.478
Okay, that sounds like fun.

07:14.517 --> 07:15.717
Oh, my God.

07:15.752 --> 07:17.052
Chris is dating
a Barrington.

07:17.086 --> 07:18.654
Who are the
Barringtons?

07:18.688 --> 07:20.689
They're the richest family
in all of Rhode Island.

07:20.723 --> 07:22.791
(gasps)
I must notify Gossip Girl!

07:22.826 --> 07:26.161
"Pass this along
to Gossip Girl."

07:26.196 --> 07:27.396
(phone vibrates)

07:27.430 --> 07:29.298
(gasps)

07:29.332 --> 07:30.331
(phone vibrates)

07:30.365 --> 07:32.900
(gasps)

07:32.935 --> 07:34.035
(phone vibrates)

07:34.069 --> 07:36.037
(gasps)

07:36.071 --> 07:37.038
(phone vibrates)

07:37.072 --> 07:38.573
(gasps)

07:38.607 --> 07:40.708
(phone vibrates)

07:40.742 --> 07:43.145
It's me. I'm Gossip Girl.

07:49.749 --> 07:53.035
I still can't believe Chris
is dating a Barrington.

07:53.069 --> 07:54.586
They own this whole club.

07:54.621 --> 07:56.505
Yeah, look at
all this luxury.

07:56.539 --> 07:59.240
It's like being in
a gay guy's dream.

08:00.910 --> 08:02.477
Enjoying the view?

08:02.512 --> 08:03.895
It's glorious, Edwin.

08:03.930 --> 08:05.213
Would you like
another salad bowl

08:05.247 --> 08:06.565
of chocolate-covered oysters?

08:06.599 --> 08:07.666
Is that gay enough?

08:07.700 --> 08:08.884
And then some.

08:08.918 --> 08:11.153
This has been the gayest
vacation I've ever had.

08:11.187 --> 08:14.056
I love smelling me
on your breath.

08:14.090 --> 08:15.474
Peter, what are
you doing here?

08:15.508 --> 08:16.591
You're not a member!

08:16.609 --> 08:18.176
And that means me
and the other jocks

08:18.211 --> 08:19.628
get to throw you
in the pool.

08:19.662 --> 08:21.063
Hey, Banks, Duffy,
get over here!

08:21.097 --> 08:22.698
This guy's going
for a swim.

08:22.732 --> 08:24.066
Grab him!

08:24.100 --> 08:25.734
(groaning)

08:25.768 --> 08:27.052
All right,
you're kind of heavy,

08:27.086 --> 08:28.837
so-so-so
we're gonna pee on you.

08:28.871 --> 08:30.872
(zippers zip)

08:32.442 --> 08:33.742
Not happening.

08:33.776 --> 08:35.677
All right, all right,
we'll just spit on you.

08:35.712 --> 08:37.713
(lips smacking)

08:40.600 --> 08:42.668
Oh, nothing we have works.

08:42.702 --> 08:45.303
Daddy, we're here to have
brunch with the Barringtons.

08:45.338 --> 08:47.539
The Barringtons?!
How is that possible?

08:47.573 --> 08:49.608
That family is the pinnacle
of high society.

08:49.642 --> 08:51.343
They-they haven't worked
in eight generations.

08:51.377 --> 08:52.844
All the kids have drug problems.

08:52.879 --> 08:54.346
Most of them have O.D.'d.

08:54.380 --> 08:55.714
That's terrible.

08:55.748 --> 08:57.215
Well, not all kids
make it, Lois.

08:57.250 --> 08:59.167
Just ask the
Sugar Smacks frog.

08:59.202 --> 09:01.920
I'm sorry, I'm afraid
you've lost two more.

09:01.954 --> 09:03.655
What should we do
about the graves?

09:03.690 --> 09:04.923
Dig 'em.

09:09.363 --> 09:11.364
You look really
handsome today, Chris.

09:11.398 --> 09:12.699
Thanks, Amanda.

09:12.733 --> 09:13.966
STEWIE:
Hey, Chris, say it.

09:14.001 --> 09:16.402
I use Stewart Griffin
Facial Cleanser.

09:16.437 --> 09:17.437
Try some.

09:17.471 --> 09:18.571
Give her
the Web site.

09:18.605 --> 09:20.606
StewieGriffinFacial.com.

09:20.641 --> 09:22.108
No, no, no,
th-th-that's something else.

09:22.142 --> 09:25.144
It's
StewieGriffinFacialCleanser.com.

09:25.179 --> 09:26.512
Hey, listen,
Mr. Barrington,

09:26.547 --> 09:28.614
y-your granddaughter
ain't no tease, right?

09:28.649 --> 09:30.289
'Cause Chris really
wants to get in there.

09:30.317 --> 09:32.452
Oh, you're a funny guy,
Griffin.

09:32.486 --> 09:33.720
I like that.

09:33.754 --> 09:35.822
Oh, well, you should hear
my prank phone calls.

09:35.856 --> 09:37.590
(dialing)

09:37.624 --> 09:39.759
Hey,
is your refrigerator running?

09:39.793 --> 09:40.927
MAN:
Yes, it is.

09:40.961 --> 09:42.528
Are your doors unlocked?

09:42.563 --> 09:44.163
What? Why?

09:48.068 --> 09:50.169
I don't know, they all
kind of look the same.

09:50.204 --> 09:53.639
What do you mean "they
all look the same"?

09:54.775 --> 09:57.410
Hey, there's all
my favorite people!

09:57.444 --> 09:59.345
Oh, no, not this suck-up.

09:59.379 --> 10:00.713
What are we talking about?

10:00.748 --> 10:02.181
Black people? Mexicans?

10:02.216 --> 10:04.117
Jews? (laughs)

10:04.151 --> 10:05.852
So good to see you,
Barrington.

10:05.886 --> 10:07.420
Hey, hey, where we going today,
Reginald?

10:07.454 --> 10:08.688
Huh? Huh?
Where we going today?

10:08.722 --> 10:10.089
You and me is pals,
ain't we, Reginald?

10:10.124 --> 10:11.524
Pewterschmidt,
settle down!

10:11.558 --> 10:13.993
I was having a nice
conversation with Peter.

10:14.027 --> 10:16.262
Uh, Peter, why don't you tell me
more about your job.

10:16.296 --> 10:17.897
You said you like
to drink at work?

10:17.931 --> 10:19.031
I do.
Oh, me, too!

10:19.066 --> 10:20.199
Me, too.
I'll drink anything.

10:20.234 --> 10:21.874
Even that hollandaise sauce.
Give me that.

10:23.837 --> 10:25.238
(screams)

10:25.272 --> 10:27.473
Hey, Brian,
Meg's Benedict.

10:27.508 --> 10:30.877
(forced laughter)

10:30.911 --> 10:32.211
Oh, God.
Ho, ho, ho.

10:32.246 --> 10:33.379
Stop. Stop.

10:33.413 --> 10:35.014
Stop.
I'm sorry I even said it.

10:35.048 --> 10:36.482
I'm so...
It was a mistake.

10:36.517 --> 10:38.417
It was a mistake.
I'm sorry I said it.

10:38.452 --> 10:41.120
Peter, why don't you
and I grab some air, huh?

10:41.155 --> 10:43.489
Daddy, you're making a
fool out of yourself.

10:43.524 --> 10:44.991
Why are you
acting like this?

10:45.025 --> 10:46.325
Look, I've been
trying to get

10:46.360 --> 10:48.494
into Reginald Barrington's
inner circle for years.

10:48.529 --> 10:50.196
They've been
the most elite family

10:50.230 --> 10:51.931
in this country
ever since it was founded.

10:51.965 --> 10:54.600
They were the ones who invented
the buckle on the hat.

10:54.635 --> 10:56.035
Hey, I like
your zipper hat.

10:56.069 --> 10:57.570
I like your zipper hat.

10:57.604 --> 10:59.071
Morning, fellas.

10:59.106 --> 11:02.575
Oh, that's gonna
be a game changer.

11:02.609 --> 11:04.477
Do you hunt, Peter?

11:04.511 --> 11:07.113
Well, I went to three
stores to find this shirt.

11:07.147 --> 11:09.215
(laughs)
Peter, you-you've got moxie.

11:09.249 --> 11:10.383
I like that.

11:10.417 --> 11:12.084
Hey, I've got moxie, too!
Watch this!

11:12.119 --> 11:14.420
♪ Carmen Miranda,
Carmen Miranda ♪

11:14.454 --> 11:15.822
♪ Was she a singer?

11:15.856 --> 11:17.089
♪ Was she a dancer?

11:17.124 --> 11:18.357
♪ Nobody knows

11:18.392 --> 11:20.026
♪ They just remember
the fruit. ♪

11:20.060 --> 11:22.328
Pewterschmidt,
you imbecile!

11:22.362 --> 11:24.397
You think that's funny,
wasting fruit?

11:24.431 --> 11:26.566
There are people dying
in hilarious places.

11:26.600 --> 11:27.667
That is it!

11:27.701 --> 11:30.102
You are officially
kicked out of this club!

11:30.137 --> 11:31.237
What?

11:31.271 --> 11:32.772
Griffin,
we just had an opening.

11:32.806 --> 11:35.241
Congratulations,
you are now a member.

11:35.275 --> 11:36.676
Oh, my God, really?

11:36.710 --> 11:38.778
And to think,
yesterday I was just a guy

11:38.812 --> 11:40.513
at home eating catnip.

11:50.290 --> 11:51.757
Excuse me, Mr. Pewterschmidt,

11:51.792 --> 11:53.760
but you're no longer
a member at this club.

11:53.795 --> 11:55.128
Don't worry,
he's my guest.

11:55.163 --> 11:56.530
Now, look, Peter,

11:56.564 --> 11:58.732
j-just because you're
a member now and I'm your guest,

11:58.766 --> 12:01.034
that doesn't mean things are
gonna change between us, right?

12:01.069 --> 12:02.436
No, no, of course not.

12:02.470 --> 12:04.605
Excuse me a
moment, Carter.

12:04.639 --> 12:07.374
Hey, guys, I just bumped into
Carter Pewterschmidt outside.

12:07.408 --> 12:08.642
What a loser, huh?

12:08.676 --> 12:09.977
(laughter)

12:10.011 --> 12:11.278
Okay, when he
wasn't looking,

12:11.312 --> 12:13.513
I stuck a springy
snake in his wallet.

12:13.548 --> 12:15.215
What? Aah!

12:15.250 --> 12:16.884
And I switched out
one of his eyeballs

12:16.918 --> 12:18.385
for a gag
exploding eyeball.

12:18.419 --> 12:19.553
What? That's impossib...

12:19.587 --> 12:20.621
Aah!

12:20.655 --> 12:22.256
And then I paid a
couple of Mexicans

12:22.290 --> 12:24.291
to run over him
with their car.

12:25.760 --> 12:27.895
I hope they don't just take
the money and skip town.

12:30.732 --> 12:32.132
Okay, you ready
for some polo?

12:32.166 --> 12:33.667
All right,
this is more like it.

12:33.701 --> 12:34.668
Where's Buttercup?

12:34.702 --> 12:36.470
Oh, only members
can ride Buttercup.

12:36.504 --> 12:39.306
Guests have to ride Topsy
the Roid Rage Horse.

12:39.340 --> 12:40.674
(snorts)

12:40.708 --> 12:42.743
Now, whatever you do,
don't say his trigger word.

12:42.777 --> 12:44.878
What?
Aah! That's his trigger word!

12:44.913 --> 12:46.847
(screaming)

12:46.881 --> 12:48.615
Don't yell! His parents
were slaughtered by yellers.

12:48.650 --> 12:49.650
Just submit.

12:49.684 --> 12:51.318
I am submitting!
It's getting worse!

12:51.352 --> 12:52.719
No, I mean really submit.

12:52.754 --> 12:54.187
Okay, okay!

12:54.222 --> 12:55.889
Oh, my God,
I meant say you're sorry,

12:55.924 --> 12:57.557
not take off your pants.

12:57.592 --> 12:59.927
Carter, what are you doing?
Oh, my God!

12:59.961 --> 13:02.095
And now that I've made you aware
of the misunderstanding,

13:02.130 --> 13:03.597
you're still continuing with it.

13:03.631 --> 13:05.699
Oh, my God!
And I'm still watching.

13:05.733 --> 13:07.000
What's wrong with me?

13:07.035 --> 13:08.669
Oh, my God!

13:12.073 --> 13:15.843
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Game of Thrones on BET.</i>

13:15.878 --> 13:18.379
I got a big-ass coat,
chair to sit in,

13:18.414 --> 13:20.581
chalice cup of wine
and a midget,

13:20.616 --> 13:21.916
but I ain't going out there

13:21.951 --> 13:23.718
with all them monsters
out there!

13:23.752 --> 13:26.321
(sobbing)

13:26.355 --> 13:28.221
Daddy, what
happened to you?

13:28.256 --> 13:30.424
I can't live
without the country club.

13:30.458 --> 13:31.491
You did this, Peter!

13:31.526 --> 13:32.626
This is all your fault!

13:32.660 --> 13:34.227
I like your hair.
Well, Daddy,

13:34.262 --> 13:36.229
you've been treating
Peter like dirt for years.

13:36.264 --> 13:38.532
It's-it's choppier;
it's more texturized.

13:38.566 --> 13:40.968
Did you go to the Asian
guy with the one name?

13:41.002 --> 13:42.836
Well, now that you
know how it feels,

13:42.870 --> 13:44.638
maybe you want to
give him an apology.

13:44.672 --> 13:45.939
You went to Taki,
didn't you?

13:45.974 --> 13:48.375
Look, Peter, I'm sorry
for the way I treated you,

13:48.409 --> 13:51.311
but is there anything you can do
to get me back in the club?

13:51.346 --> 13:52.980
Well, I suppose I could
talk to Barrington.

13:53.014 --> 13:54.348
Really? Oh, Peter,

13:54.382 --> 13:55.983
you don't know
what this means to me.

13:56.017 --> 13:58.452
Oh, you know, I was so desperate
there for a while,

13:58.486 --> 13:59.720
I even tried a Jewish club.

13:59.754 --> 14:01.121
Oh, you don't want
to get involved

14:01.155 --> 14:02.289
with them
religious groups.

14:02.323 --> 14:04.358
They believe in all
kinds of weird stuff.

14:04.392 --> 14:06.126
If I believe
in Jesus hard enough,

14:06.160 --> 14:07.828
I will not die.

14:07.862 --> 14:09.863
If I believe
in Snake Jesus hard enough,

14:09.897 --> 14:11.164
he will die.

14:11.199 --> 14:13.333
If I believe
in Tree Jesus hard enough,

14:13.368 --> 14:14.801
both of them will die.

14:14.836 --> 14:16.236
(thunder booms)

14:16.270 --> 14:18.772
Yay! Thank you, Tree Jesus!

14:18.806 --> 14:20.607
(gunfire)

14:20.641 --> 14:22.442
Hey, Mr. Barrington.

14:22.477 --> 14:23.543
Oh, hello, Peter.

14:23.578 --> 14:24.845
I'm so glad you're here.

14:24.879 --> 14:27.247
We're shooting bald guys
under five-seven today.

14:27.281 --> 14:28.749
Hey, there's the guy

14:28.783 --> 14:30.417
who denied
my health insurance claim.

14:30.451 --> 14:31.952
Sir, your nipples are fine!

14:31.986 --> 14:33.987
You don't need
to reconstruct them!

14:34.022 --> 14:37.190
I want Hershey Kiss nipples,
and I want you to pay for them!

14:37.225 --> 14:39.026
Look, Mr. B.,
if it's okay with you,

14:39.060 --> 14:41.362
I'd like to give
my membership back to Carter.

14:41.397 --> 14:43.197
I'm sorry, Peter, but
I just don't think

14:43.232 --> 14:45.099
Pewterschmidt is
country club material.

14:45.134 --> 14:46.300
Now if you'll excuse me,

14:46.335 --> 14:48.536
I'm about to shoot
Michael Stipe.

14:48.570 --> 14:50.138
(chuckles)
Is that...

14:50.172 --> 14:51.439
Is that him
in the corner?

14:51.473 --> 14:52.874
Yes, that is him
in the corner.

14:52.908 --> 14:54.542
Is that him
in the spotlight?

14:54.576 --> 14:55.977
Would you...
Oh, damn it!

14:56.011 --> 14:57.145
Now he got away!

14:57.179 --> 14:59.047
Oh, no...
I said too much?

14:59.081 --> 15:00.681
I want you
out of here!

15:00.716 --> 15:02.650
Look, Mr. Barrington,
he's my father-in-law.

15:02.684 --> 15:04.585
So if he goes, I go.

15:04.620 --> 15:06.220
Fine, I don't care.

15:06.255 --> 15:08.856
Your low-brow antics no
longer amuse me, Griffin.

15:08.891 --> 15:10.358
You're both out
of the club.

15:10.392 --> 15:11.959
Well, I guess that's it then.

15:11.994 --> 15:14.062
Oh, there is one
more thing, actually.

15:14.096 --> 15:16.230
Can you talk to that
angry little boy

15:16.265 --> 15:17.732
down by the river bank?

15:17.766 --> 15:20.168
Uh, yeah, sure.

15:24.173 --> 15:25.573
Hey, what's eating you?

15:25.607 --> 15:26.707
Grown-ups.

15:26.742 --> 15:28.376
Yeah, grown-ups suck.

15:28.410 --> 15:30.478
Why do they get to make
all the rules?

15:30.512 --> 15:32.547
I know it seems
unfair, but, hey,

15:32.581 --> 15:34.415
there ain't no rules
in a tickle fight.

15:34.450 --> 15:35.917
(laughter)
Stop!

15:35.951 --> 15:37.752
You're tickling!

15:37.786 --> 15:39.220
Timmy, there you are!

15:39.254 --> 15:40.721
Who the (bleep)
are you?!

15:40.756 --> 15:42.156
Get away from our son!

15:42.191 --> 15:43.491
But Mr. Barrington
told me to...

15:43.525 --> 15:44.859
Who's Mr. Barrington?

15:44.893 --> 15:46.694
From the club.
What club?

15:46.728 --> 15:48.362
You're in a lot
of trouble, mister.

15:48.397 --> 15:49.497
(screams)

15:55.649 --> 15:57.884
I'm sorry I got us both
kicked out, Carter.

15:57.918 --> 15:59.552
I was just trying
to help you out.

15:59.586 --> 16:02.288
Mr. Barrington told me
I couldn't see Amanda anymore.

16:02.322 --> 16:04.725
We never even got
a chance to have sex.

16:04.759 --> 16:08.245
Everyone knows rich, Waspy girls
are the best at it.

16:08.279 --> 16:10.080
I'm really gonna miss that club.

16:10.114 --> 16:11.832
You know what part
I liked the most?

16:11.866 --> 16:13.567
Walking around
the locker room naked

16:13.601 --> 16:16.637
and offering people sections
of a tiny clementine.

16:16.671 --> 16:17.905
Clementine?

16:17.939 --> 16:19.523
Oh, thank you.

16:19.557 --> 16:20.774
Clementine?

16:20.808 --> 16:21.792
None for
me, thanks.

16:21.843 --> 16:22.876
Clementine?

16:22.910 --> 16:24.678
Yes, thank you.

16:24.712 --> 16:26.046
Clementine?
Yeah, I'll have one.

16:26.080 --> 16:27.430
Ooh, softly.
Sorry.

16:27.464 --> 16:28.848
(quietly):
Yes, I'll have one.

16:28.882 --> 16:30.650
There you go.

16:30.684 --> 16:33.786
God, it's good
to be old and nude.

16:33.820 --> 16:35.755
Look, Carter,
you can't be that surprised.

16:35.789 --> 16:37.023
I mean,
it's just human nature

16:37.057 --> 16:38.641
to suck up to the people
above you,

16:38.675 --> 16:41.010
crap on those beneath you
and undercut your equals.

16:41.044 --> 16:42.778
Well, then we just
got to figure out a way

16:42.813 --> 16:44.113
to make you fancier
than Barrington,

16:44.147 --> 16:45.748
so he's got
to suck up to you.

16:45.782 --> 16:46.882
I don't know, Peter.

16:46.917 --> 16:48.334
That'd be pretty
tough to pull off.

16:48.368 --> 16:49.619
We just got to be bold.

16:49.653 --> 16:51.687
Like those
backwards-knee birds.

16:52.706 --> 16:53.706
Oh, what? What?

16:53.740 --> 16:55.241
Oh, what? What are
you looking at?

16:55.275 --> 16:56.442
Oh, you coming for me?

16:56.460 --> 16:57.910
No, no, I'll just take

16:57.944 --> 17:00.296
a big backward-knee step
in the opposite direction.

17:00.330 --> 17:02.398
Yeah, yeah, you think
I'm afraid of you?

17:02.432 --> 17:05.701
I slept on your back
last night, you (bleep).

17:10.407 --> 17:11.874
Yes, I'll have
the filet mignon,

17:11.908 --> 17:13.909
and they can start
the sunset now.

17:13.944 --> 17:16.178
(helicopter approaches)

17:16.229 --> 17:17.897
Someone important
must be arriving

17:17.931 --> 17:20.132
because they're making
a big entrance.

17:34.749 --> 17:36.333
(bugle plays)

17:36.367 --> 17:39.319
Announcing the arrival
of His and His Majesty,

17:39.354 --> 17:41.455
the exceedingly wealthy
and very important

17:41.489 --> 17:43.690
Viscount James Earl
Tennis Racquet,

17:43.725 --> 17:45.592
and Duke of
Lacrosse Team.

17:45.626 --> 17:47.794
Hello, I'm Reginald
Barrington.

17:47.829 --> 17:49.930
Where are you fine
gentlemen from?

17:49.964 --> 17:51.164
We are European,

17:51.199 --> 17:53.133
from the United
Coloreds of Benetton.

17:53.167 --> 17:55.135
But you don't sound
like you're from Europe.

17:55.169 --> 17:56.536
Is that so?

17:56.571 --> 17:58.705
Well, perhaps I should take
my thong elsewhere.

17:58.740 --> 18:00.707
Well, let's
not be hasty.

18:00.742 --> 18:03.327
Your Majesty, won't
you please join me

18:03.361 --> 18:06.113
as my personal guests
in the Barrington Room?

18:06.147 --> 18:07.614
The Barrington Room?!

18:07.648 --> 18:10.067
Peter, that's the most exclusive
room in all of New England.

18:10.101 --> 18:12.336
Yeah, I hear it's even
harder to get in there

18:12.370 --> 18:13.870
than the University
of Arizona.

18:13.905 --> 18:15.539
Well, it's beating.

18:15.573 --> 18:18.125
Welcome to the Wildcats.

18:18.159 --> 18:20.126
This is the
Barrington Room.

18:20.144 --> 18:21.595
Have a seat in
the deepest,

18:21.629 --> 18:24.965
most luxurious leather chair
in the world.

18:26.968 --> 18:29.870
(sighs):
Oh, that's nice.

18:29.904 --> 18:32.122
Sir, may I offer you
a shoe drink?

18:32.156 --> 18:34.574
Why, yes, that'd
be lovely.

18:36.327 --> 18:38.678
(sighs):
Ah, the finer things.

18:38.713 --> 18:40.647
So, what brings
you gentlemen to town?

18:40.681 --> 18:41.865
We're here on business.

18:41.899 --> 18:43.517
In fact, we just
came from a meeting

18:43.551 --> 18:45.352
with the venerable
Carter Pewterschmidt.

18:45.386 --> 18:46.653
Outstanding man.

18:46.687 --> 18:47.921
Really? Yeah, well,

18:47.955 --> 18:50.675
he used to be a member here,
but he was very annoying.

18:50.709 --> 18:52.643
Oh, my, that's-that's
surprising.

18:52.678 --> 18:55.129
I-I've heard he has quite
the blue-blood pedigree.

18:55.164 --> 18:56.998
You know, he got a
piece of Jackie Kennedy

18:57.032 --> 18:59.634
before she was defiled by
that hairy olive-eater.

18:59.668 --> 19:01.602
Yeah, and-and
he once made me

19:01.637 --> 19:03.438
a grilled cheese
sandwich after this.

19:03.472 --> 19:05.606
Well, I wasn't sure
about Pewterschmidt,

19:05.641 --> 19:07.341
but after hearing
you gentlemen talk,

19:07.376 --> 19:09.277
maybe I could give him
another chance.

19:09.311 --> 19:10.678
Really?
Oh, wow!

19:10.712 --> 19:12.547
That's great news,
Carter. You're back in!

19:12.581 --> 19:13.998
Hey, let's get a
couple of girls

19:14.032 --> 19:16.300
and have seventh-grade-in-
the-same-room-make-outs.

19:16.335 --> 19:18.336
"Carter"? Wait a minute.

19:18.370 --> 19:20.021
You're not
Duke of Lacrosse Team!

19:20.055 --> 19:23.040
And you're not Viscount
James Earl Tennis Racquet!

19:23.075 --> 19:24.325
Security!

19:24.359 --> 19:26.526
Come throw these frauds
out of my club!

19:26.561 --> 19:27.994
Damn it, Peter,
you blew it!

19:28.029 --> 19:30.280
(screams) I knew I couldn't depend
on you!

19:30.314 --> 19:32.632
You're not worthy to lick
my designer shoes,

19:32.667 --> 19:34.000
you fat, low-life slob!

19:34.035 --> 19:35.569
But, Carter, please!

19:35.603 --> 19:38.321
Here, skip this rope and do
a lively schoolgirl chant.

19:38.356 --> 19:40.524
But, Carter, I don't know
any city girl rhymes.

19:40.558 --> 19:42.008
Do it!

19:42.042 --> 19:44.377
(chanting): Lettuce, carrots,
peppers and peas.

19:44.395 --> 19:46.897
Your mother says to
got to have these.

19:46.931 --> 19:48.682
Now do it double time
with new vegetables!

19:48.716 --> 19:50.884
Cabbage, taters,
spinach and peas.

19:50.902 --> 19:52.185
You already said "peas"!

19:52.219 --> 19:54.821
I don't know any
more vegetables.

19:54.856 --> 19:57.107
Wait a second,
hang on there.

19:57.141 --> 19:59.943
The way you abused
that man just now,

19:59.977 --> 20:01.778
the way you treated
your lesser--

20:01.813 --> 20:04.047
I underestimated you,
Pewterschmidt.

20:04.081 --> 20:06.450
I thought you were just
some suck-up loser,

20:06.484 --> 20:07.851
but you have shown me

20:07.885 --> 20:10.020
that you've got the mettle
to be one of us.

20:10.054 --> 20:11.388
You are back in the club.

20:11.422 --> 20:13.356
Oh, thank you,
Mr. Barrington!

20:13.391 --> 20:16.194
Yes. Now, I believe
there is just one last piece

20:16.228 --> 20:18.663
of unfinished business
to take care of here.

20:21.099 --> 20:23.067
(groans)

20:23.101 --> 20:25.670
I'm sorry, but the Viscount
James Earl Tennis Racquet

20:25.704 --> 20:28.439
and Duke of Lacrosse Team
already arrived two hours ago.

20:28.474 --> 20:30.875
But that's impossible!

20:34.680 --> 20:35.913
Peter, I'm sorry

20:35.948 --> 20:38.115
you've got to give up
the country club life.

20:38.150 --> 20:39.450
Oh, that's okay, Lois.

20:39.485 --> 20:40.818
'Cause you know,
I got to say,

20:40.853 --> 20:42.887
I don't think those rich guys
have it all that great.

20:42.921 --> 20:44.288
Too much stress.

20:44.323 --> 20:45.556
You know,
you give me the choice,

20:45.591 --> 20:47.258
I'll choose our life
any day of the week.

20:47.292 --> 20:48.659
Me, too, Peter.

20:48.694 --> 20:50.661
Can I have $50 to
get my hair cut?

20:50.696 --> 20:52.263
Absolutely not.
That's a waste of money.

20:52.297 --> 20:53.831
I will cut it myself.

20:53.866 --> 20:55.266
(snipping)

20:55.300 --> 20:57.568
You look like garbage.
What happened?

20:57.569 --> 21:58.569
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru